msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:621
msgid ""
"WP-Cron relies on site visits to run scheduled tasks, which can be "
"unreliable on low-traffic sites. Setting up a real server cron job is "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:623
msgid ""
"Add one of the following lines to your server crontab (runs every 15 "
"minutes):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:630
msgid "Where to paste it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:632
msgid "Shared hosting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:633
msgid ""
"Most hosting control panels (cPanel, Plesk, and most rental servers) have a "
"'Cron jobs' section. Paste the line above there. If the panel asks for "
"command and schedule separately, set the schedule to every 15 minutes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:635
msgid "VPS / dedicated server"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:636
msgid "Run `crontab -e` and paste the line above on a new line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:638
msgid "Home server"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:639
msgid ""
"If WordPress runs on your own machine, use crontab on Linux/macOS, or Task "
"Scheduler on Windows to run the command every 15 minutes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-phdrip-admin.php:641
msgid ""
"No cron settings available? Some hosts don't offer cron at all. You can "
"register the URL above with a free external ping service such as cron-"
"job.org — or simply skip this step. External cron is only an extra safety "
"net: the plugin works with the normal WordPress cron, and the built-in "
"watchdog rescues any missed posts."
msgstr ""

